@T_Okonkwo We're sorry to hear about your experience buying the Larkspur Mid-Cap Momentum ETF (LKMM) at Tuesday's open, and we appreciate you raising it. ETF shares are bought and sold at market prices, which can be higher or lower than the fund's net asset value, and bid-ask spreads can widen at the open and during volatile periods; a market order executes at the best available price at that moment, which may differ from the last price you saw. A limit order lets an investor set the maximum price they are willing to pay, although it may not be filled.

We aren't able to discuss individual trades or accounts on social media. Please contact Larkspur Shareholder Services at 1-800-555-0164 (weekdays, 8 a.m.-6 p.m. ET) or the brokerage firm that executed your order, and we will help you get the information you need. Investors should consider the fund's investment objectives, risks, charges and expenses carefully before investing; the prospectus contains this and other information and is available at larkspurfunds.example/LKMM. ETF shares may trade at a premium or discount to NAV, and investing involves risk, including loss of principal.

